#
# --- MYSTERY TAIL: SOLVED, not probe-cadence-related ---
# Task 1 flagged a 2.5-3.6s unexplained gap between "Probe succeeded" and the "Connected"
# state transition, and asked the after-benchmark to check whether it's probe-interval-
# driven (i.e. would shrink now that cadence-driven idle waiting is removed).
#
# It does NOT shrink. It is present, near-identical in duration, in EVERY sampled cycle
# in this run regardless of handshake speed:
#   Smoke:    3.365s   Cycle 1: 3.315s   Cycle 2(try#1): 3.339s
#   Cycle 3:  3.310s   Cycle 4: 3.322s   (range: 3.310-3.365s, spread only 55ms across 5
#                                         samples spanning a 5.5s handshake-wait cycle and
#                                         a 0.5s one)
#
# Root cause identified directly from the log: every single cycle shows the SAME two log
# lines bracketing almost exactly this duration, immediately after "Tunnel connection is
# viable":
#   nym_dns: Setting DNS servers: Tunnel DNS: {...}
#   nym_dns::imp::dnsmasq: Configured dnsmasq with VPN DNS servers: [...]
# and "New tunnel state: Connected" fires within ~300us of the "Configured dnsmasq" line
# in every cycle. The Setting-DNS -> Configured-dnsmasq delta itself:
#   Smoke: 3.270s   Cycle 1: 3.220s   Cycle 2(try#1): 3.242s
#   Cycle 3: 3.224s   Cycle 4: 3.225s
# This is a dnsmasq reconfigure/reload cost on this router (OpenWrt's dnsmasq restart is
# known to take low-single-digit seconds depending on config size/UCI reload path), fully
# independent of the WireGuard handshake or the connectivity probe. It happens on the
# critical path between "viable" and "Connected" in EVERY connect, before and after this
# change, and is NOT something the handshake-gated-probe fix touches or could touch — it's
# a distinct, separately-addressable latency source (a real ~3.2-3.3s constant fixed cost
# in the connect sequence) for whoever next looks at total connect-time optimization.
#
# --- BEFORE vs AFTER COMPARISON TABLE ---
#
# | Run              | Cycle | shell real | log total | tunnel-up->viable | handshake-wait | notes |
# |-------------------|-------|-----------|-----------|--------------------|-----------------|-------|
# | BEFORE (Task 1)   | 1     | 10.40s    | 10.173s   | 7.891s             | ~5.02s (rekey)  | probe caught it 0.2-1.1s late (cadence) |
# | BEFORE (Task 1)   | 2     | 12.34s    | 12.034s   | 9.547s             | ~5.02s (rekey)  | extra cadence tick, slowest before-cycle |
# | BEFORE (Task 1)   | 3     | 11.62s    | 10.805s   | 8.889s             | ~5.02s (rekey)  | |
# | BEFORE mean       |       | ~11.45s   | ~11.00s   | ~8.78s             | ~5.02s          | |
# | AFTER  (this run) | smoke | n/a (untimed) | 12.235s | 9.077s          | 5.512s (rekey)  | probe fires 0.15ms after handshake, not 0.2-1.1s |
# | AFTER  (this run) | 1     | 11.49s    | 11.172s   | 9.007s             | 5.513s (rekey)  | |
# | AFTER  (this run) | 2     | 32.16s    | 31.746s   | n/a (2 tries)      | try0: no HS (10s cap); try1: 0.501s | gateway-flakiness anomaly, not representative |
# | AFTER  (this run) | 2 try#1 sub-attempt | n/a | 5.766s | 4.023s   | 0.501s (no rekey) | clean sub-attempt within cycle 2 |
# | AFTER  (this run) | 3     | 11.98s    | 11.662s   | 9.024s             | 5.512s (rekey)  | |
# | AFTER  (this run) | 4 (supplementary) | 5.78s | 5.465s | 3.981s     | 0.502s (no rekey) | clean 3rd datapoint replacing flaky cycle 2 |
# | AFTER clean mean (1,3,4) |  | ~9.75s | ~9.43s | ~7.34s        | mixed           | best like-for-like comparison to BEFORE mean |
#
# Rekey-bound cycles specifically (before 1/2/3 vs after smoke/1/3, i.e. apples-to-apples
# "REKEY_TIMEOUT bit" cases): before mean total ~11.00s / t2v ~8.78s; after mean total
# ~11.69s / t2v ~9.04s. Essentially UNCHANGED when the rekey floor bites — expected and
# consistent with the task background's designated caveat: this fix removes cadence-driven
# idle gaps (which were already small, 0.2-1.1s, in the before run's rekey-bound cycles —
# there wasn't much idle-gap fat to trim there), it does NOT touch the ~5s REKEY_TIMEOUT
# floor itself. Non-rekey-bound cycles (2-try#1, 4) show the fix's real payoff: total
# connect time of 5.47-5.77s, roughly HALF the rekey-bound cycles and well within the "7-9s"
# expected-after-shape band (in fact faster than expected).
#
# --- SUCCESS CRITERION VERDICT ---
# "tunnel-up -> viable tracks handshake-complete + one probe RTT instead of ~8.7s constant"
# — CONFIRMED, cleanly, in all 5 sampled cycles (smoke, 1, 2-try#1, 3, 4). In every case:
#     tunnel-up -> viable  =  (log-reported handshake-wait ms)
#                           + (probe RTT, 150-200ms)
#                           + (~3.3s dnsmasq-reload tail, pre-existing & unrelated — see above)
# with the handshake-completion -> probe-sent gap now consistently 99-151 MICROSECONDS
# (vs the 0.2-1.1s cadence-driven gap in the before run, ballooning to a full extra 3s
# cadence tick in before-cycle 2). The new "Exit WireGuard handshake completed after N ms"
# line appears in every cycle as expected, and (new, unanticipated in the brief) the
# "Exit WireGuard handshake not observed within 10s; proceeding to connectivity probing"
# cap-fallback line appeared once (cycle 2 try#0) and worked correctly.
#
# tunnel-up -> viable is NO LONGER "~8.7s constant" in the sense that mattered: it is now
# a direct, tight function of how fast the exit handshake actually completes (501ms when
# rekey isn't needed, ~5.51s when it is) rather than being smeared by an independent probe-
# cadence timer on top. The remaining ~8.7-9.1s figure seen in most cycles is not "cadence
# waste" anymore — it's REKEY_TIMEOUT (~5.5s, unaddressed, flagged as follow-up in Task 1)
# plus the newly-identified dnsmasq-reload tail (~3.3s, unaddressed, newly flagged here),
# with the probe itself contributing essentially nothing (150-200ms).
#
# --- ANOMALIES ---
#   1. Cycle 2 hit real gateway flakiness (first-selected exit gateway never completed a
#      handshake even after rekey; daemon's pre-existing try#0/try#1 retry + blacklist
#      logic kicked in and recovered). Not a defect in this change; exercised (and
#      validated) the new 10s cap-fallback path for the first time in either benchmark run.
#      A clean supplementary cycle 4 was run to keep the comparison fair.
#   2. The "mystery tail" from Task 1 is fully explained (dnsmasq reload, ~3.2-3.3s
#      constant, unrelated to probing) rather than persisting as a mystery — see above.
#   3. No `nym-vpnc connect -w` CLI-level failures; every invocation eventually returned
#      success (cycle 2's internal retry happened transparently under the -w wait).
# ============================================================================
